  "term": "productive thinking",
  "definition": "Productive thinking is a cognitive process that brings together creative and critical thinking to produce solutions that are new, effective, and suited to the situation. It involves skills used to examine a problem, generate different possibilities, and turn ideas into practical outcomes.",
